---
/**
 * Representative rendered-Markdown body used by the accessibility (axe-core)
 * tests (task 20.1). It stands in for the HTML that Astro's Markdown pipeline
 * (`render(entry)`) hands to `NoteContent.astro` as its `Content` component, so
 * the a11y audit runs over markup shaped like a real Note without booting the
 * whole content collection / build.
 *
 * It deliberately exercises the rich elements a Note can contain — headings
 * (starting at h2, below the Note's h1), paragraphs, links, inline + block
 * code, ordered/unordered lists, a blockquote, a data table, and images — and
 * it models the two image cases the accessibility requirements distinguish:
 *   - a content image carrying descriptive alt text (Req 7.4), and
 *   - a decorative image marked so assistive tech ignores it, i.e. alt=""
 *     (Req 7.5).
 * The headings descend one level at a time so the audit's heading-order check
 * is meaningful rather than accidentally violated by the scaffold.
 */
---

